From efd6edcbe6ae52751dcb13e1ec8ba46905f59ccd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pleft <elefasgr@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:10:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/16] Add usb2dc_superpico: Dreamcast adapter on a Watara
 SuperPico, with a PSP as the controller

A build target for the SuperPico flash cart (a Raspberry Pi Pico behind three
always-enabled 74LVC245 buffers on GP0-GP16 and GP28): Maple on GP21/GP22,
debug UART1 TX on GP20, nothing driven on the buffered pins.

A TinyUSB host class driver (usb/usbh/psp2dc, CONFIG_PSP2DC) for a Sony PSP
running the PSP2DC application over PSPExp's USB link (054c:01ca, vendor
class, bulk IN + OUT): half duplex, since the RP2040 host runs one
non-interrupt transfer at a time. The protocol header lives in the PSP2DC
project (../../protocol/psp2dc_protocol.h).

Tested on hardware: a PSP-1000 navigating GDMENU and playing Crazy Taxi 2 on
a real Dreamcast.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
